schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: RID (Reference Identifier)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A stable label that points to a knowledge object (doc, message, record)
    without handing over the object itself — like a library call number.
  source_traditions:
    - KOI-net protocol (BlockScience, with Metagov and RMIT)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    The mechanism cited as enabling federation without consolidation:
    organizations share the RID (the label/pointer) while keeping the
    underlying content and access rules under their own control. Attributed
    to BlockScience's Michael Zargham and Ilan Ben-Meir: "a stable concept
    of a reference as something distinct from (but referring to) an
    underlying referent is thus the mechanism that enables organizations to
    interoperate while retaining (and securing) their respective boundaries."
  adjacent_meanings:
    - federation
    - koi-net
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      reference-vs-referent — the RID is the pointer/label; the referent
      (the actual document/message/record) is never itself transferred
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Only quoting the RID concept without KOI-net's supporting node roles
    (sensor/processor/coordinator) can make it sound like a naming scheme
    alone accomplishes federation; the roles are what actually move and
    transform the referenced knowledge across a network.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/federation-portability.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
